{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e","id":74082,"title":"What should each Purview do in 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T21:01:48-08:00","id":74082,"title":"What should each Purview do in 2e?","content":"So, I've been turning this topic in my head for a while. While I'm not sure what's currently being discussed among the Onyx Path people and how Purviews are gonna change, I wanted to start a discussion about the various Purviews as we know them and what sorts of Boons those Purviews should offer, based on what gods with those powers can do in mythology... <br /> <br /> So, I'm gonna start with Fertility, because it's a common associated Purview in divine parents (every pantheon has at least one), it's a cool, mythically thematic concept, and also one that many Scion players dislike because few powers in it are really effective or consistently useful. Also, I personally think that if any Purview needs a rename, this is it, just to clarify that this purview has everything to do with plants and the like, and nothing to do with childbirth, which is over in Health. Perhaps Flora? <br /> <br /> So, the first thing that Fertility gods are in charge of is <b>Agriculture</b>. This is the big'un. Everyone loves you when you're the one providing them with their next meal (or else is VERY eager to appease you if you've the power to take it away). This is the most important role for Fertility gods while simultaneously being the least impressive one to game. Deities like Demeter embodying the harvest, or Quetzalcoatl teaching humans to cultivate plants are highly necessary to ensuring survival of the civilization, and the first three 1e Hero Boons were all about that. And they were also very, very circumstantial and not really worth the XP. However, there's room for growth, thanks to folks like Idunn, the Norse Goddess who tends the golden apples of immortality. Making a huge geographic region flourish with crops or suffer endless blight is one thing, by the time you reach God, you should have the ability to provide divine food, creating crops that change those who eat it.<br /> <br /> From Agriculture, we have those gods who represent <b>Specific Plants</b>. These are those who represent an important plant, usually harvested as a crop, the way that Animal focuses on a specific totem beast. Aztec, Maya, and other Mesoamerican pantheons have several dozen deities who are all about corn and corn alone. The Incas have a number of lesser deities who focus on a specific crop, such as Axomama, Zaramama, Quinoamama, and Cocamama, goddesses of potatoes, maize corn, quinoa, and coca leaves respectively. I think there should be a boon that's essentially a reverse of Protean Understanding for this, wherein your Fertility god chooses a plant of some sort, and gets a sweet bonus when using Fertility Boons on that plant (with a subsequent penalty for all others). <br /> <br /> And speaking of Cocamama, she joins other plant specific deities like Xochipilli with his psychedelic mushrooms and especially Dionysus with his grapes in being gods of <b>Inebriation</b>. Dionysus may be the most popular in this area, but there are many gods of the plants people ingest to alter their states of consciousness. And, from communion wine to peyote ceremonies, drugs have been a key part of religious ceremonies across the globe. There needs to be a way for a Scion to harness that power. Toxic Thorn from Companion is a good start to this (I tried to check, not many poison-based fertility gods, outside of a few myths in Africa and the Amazon. Most poisonous divinities tend to be animalistic, like Serket's scorpions or the Midgard Serpent)<br /> <br /> From here, we're getting to a totally different direction, going from Agriculture to <b>Wilderness</b>. Rather than the gods of human-based crops, these are the gods of Fertility unfettered. This is where we get gods like Pan, Cernunnos, or the orisha Oshossi. These are gods who embody the wild part of nature, the imposing trees, the creeping vines, the thorns, the rashes, the general unpleasantness. This is where Boons like Natural Camouflage belong. Gods who take Fertility travel through the thickets and brambles without harm, evade detection among the greenery, and get people lost in an impenetrable sea of trees. <br /> <br /> And, last, we come to a huge deal with Fertility, one that has no Boons associated with it in RAW. I refer of course, to the <b>Seasonal Cycle</b>. Fertility gods embody the changes in the seasons, lesser deities sometimes having sway only during their assigned time of year. And, of course, the most extreme case of this are the deities that die in the winter and return to life in the spring. Most of the cases where gods are killed and are restored tend to be gods of Fertility. Osiris, Xipe Totec, Tammuz, to a certain extent Persephone, all embody that concept of the god that dies with the crops and is reborn with them. I feel a Boon like GBN's Circle of Life fits that. I also think that there should be ways to reflect seasonality in Boons and also to further embody that tenacity represented by plant life. <br /> <br /> Now, some might think that steps on the toes of Stamina, particularly Ultimate Stamina, but I honestly don't think so. For example, Osiris is a god of Fertility who is restored from death, but does not return to the realm of the living, so he's not rocking Ultimate Stamina. Likewise, Tammuz isn't particularly hardy in Mesopotamian myth, yet he spends half the year in the underworld to represent winter. And on the other hand, Odin and Shango both have famous myths where they kill themselves and return to life, but they're not Fertility figures in the slightest. However, certain figures clearly do have both, like Xipe Totec stoically flaying himself along with the rebirth cycle, or Dionysus being able to hold amazing amounts of liquor. Deities like that should be able to rely on both Stamina and Fertility to do their job. <br /> <br /> So, that's one Purview, I'd post more, but long post is long. Please, discuss, add more ideas as to what you think Purviews in 2e should accomplish, or criticize mine. When I next get the opportunity, I'll discuss Health","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T22:12:25-08:00","id":74122,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the a crafting Purview &quot;<i><b>Artifice</b></i>&quot; that not only allows you to make stuff &amp; craft without tools but one that allows you to craft magical wonders like Nuada's Silverhand. Crafting always seems to get the short stick, usually just making things easier to make, increasing your productivity but ultimately not giving you powerful things. Most of the time I don't need to make a thousand spears in a day, I need a spear that strikes a thousand times. I want to make wonders. Baba Yaga's hut, Perseus's Adamant Sword. Give me crafting rules that are deep &amp; wide enough to make things that aren't just upgraded armor, or pale shadows of stronger well known Artifacts like <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mj\u00f6lnir</b></span></span>, give me the rules to forge my own legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","user":"Aermas","date":". 02-18-2014, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T22:17:49-08:00","id":74128,"title":"","content":"Mm... that's just writing your own custom Relics, really. There does absolutely need to be a system in place for forging Relics, and there needs to be a Forge/Creation/Artistry/Industry/Artifice Purview that covers building magical things, but they don't need to be the same thing.<br /> <br /> There's a system for handling combat, which can be affected by many different powers from many sources. Same thing here. There needs to be a basic <i>system</i> in place that covers building items. Then the Forge Purview can modify and affect that system, just like the War Purview modifies and affects the combat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T23:01:34-08:00","id":74136,"title":"","content":"I'd like to get a purview relating to, rather than Fertility per se, Wealth or Business. Wealth gods are the ones you pray to before a big IPO. They're the ones whose symbols adorn trade caravans. There have been a few homebrew attempts to do something like this, but I'd like to see an official one.<br /> <br /> Also dreams. There needs to be a dreams purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T17:03:10-08:00","id":74643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I've been turning this topic in my head for a while. While I'm not sure what's currently being discussed among the Onyx Path people and how Purviews are gonna change, I wanted to start a discussion about the various Purviews as we know them and what sorts of Boons those Purviews should offer, based on what gods with those powers can do in mythology... </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent idea. Fertility just seemed like a random assortment of powers that got thrown together, not even the cohesive themes Griffinguy24 just discussed. And the other one that was a random assortment was...<br /> <br /> <b>Stars</b><br /> <br /> Are we about the Celestial Lights, Navigation, Portents/Divination, or Time here? The boons seem to randomly flit between screwing with time (which should really be its own purview seeing as how there are actual TIME gods) and smashing the enemy with space. Portents and/or Divination belong in Prophecy and/or Mystery. Navigation and celestial lights should be all that's actually In the Stars purview.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, i fully agree that there should be a dream Purview, and not scattered dream powers in a handful of random purviews liek before. They released that info on the Key of Morpheus and the first thing I thought was &quot;how do these mere mortals have powers the gods do not?!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 02-18-2014, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T21:11:35-08:00","id":74771,"title":"","content":"Well, to be fair, the Stars purview is 90% fanmade (if I'm reading the color coding on gothambynight correctly). There were four canon versions presented in Yazatas, and then ten created by gothambynight, and the canon ones all have to do with the &quot;brightness&quot; of stars; one boots appearance related shenanigans, another is basically a sun purview trick and makes you super bright, another throws you into space, and one makes you luckier. The prophecy/portent, time, navigation and drawing down stars and starstuff is all noncanon, and the only prophecy related Stars boon I recall just gives you a bonus on a Prophecy roll or something like that.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why there weren't Time portents and it made me really sad, because time-related characters are my favorites to play. ): Though most gods of time are actually closely related to the seasonal cycles inherent to agriculture. Kronos, the oft cited Greek god of Time, is actually an agricultural God, not strictly related to the passage of time.<br /> <br /> I think space fits stars, though, since, y'know, space-as-in-that-star-filled-void, but honestly, Navigation and celestial lights aren't even really in the Stars purview. What we have are some generally less harmful versions of the Sun purview.<br /> <br /> Tying stars to fate would make sense to me, too, though; while Prophecy and Mystery are about divining the unknown, Stars might actually be used to meddle with fate as a known force. Though if you play it right, constellations and celestial lights could already be really cool as a purview. And Navigation is just what stars are for, yeah.<br /> <br /> /sorry, stars and time are just the only purviews I care about seeing! Well, I like the darkness purviews.<br /> <br /> I think I would have liked if the Moon purview were more about moon related things than it was though. The canon powers, like Smoking Mirror, Phase Body, and Phase Cloak all struck me as kind of weird, and less tied with the mythology than, for instance, the fan created Moon Letters; sleeping would be a very good thing to base them off of, since most Moon deities are associated with sleep and dreams as well, though sleeping would probably fall more under the dream purview. . . .<br /> <br /> Ah, I have a lot of critiques but I haven't been around long enough to form coherent suggestions yet, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T21:49:43-08:00","id":74781,"title":"","content":"Artifice...seriously I so badly wanted to play a Forge god and everything seem so kludged together. Also I hope if its made its not wholly tied to Intelligence. I mean there are innovating and inventive gods, and then there are gods good at making the same things. (Really good at it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:13:01-08:00","id":74791,"title":"","content":"^ This &amp; the fact that the Super Intelligence abilities were basically &quot;You learn gooder&quot; I mean, where was all the interesting things one could do with Super Intelligence? Like compile a library in your own headspace, multitask everything, predict combat, actually scheme things etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T22:22:46-08:00","id":74794,"title":"","content":"Part of the issue with high-intelligence characters is that they present a pair of roleplay problems. On the one hand, it's really hard to roleplay a character whose brain can make connections between facts that the player cannot, kind of a reverse metagaming. On the other hand, it can lead to &quot;I roll INT to figure out the problem&quot; which I don't find particularly satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T17:45:24-08:00","id":81840,"title":"","content":"For a new Purview, I would like to see a Time Purview because that would be a welcome addition to a god's rep. An idea that I had a one time is that Chronos escaped Tartarus and transformed himself into Tik-Tok, the Olympian god of Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T18:21:47-08:00","id":81852,"title":"","content":"A time purview would be interesting, but I feel like it'd be almost impossible to manage from a ST perspective when you start having to deal with alterations to causality and potential paradoxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:40:40-08:00","id":81938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=81852#post81852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A time purview would be interesting, but I feel like it'd be almost impossible to manage from a ST perspective when you start having to deal with alterations to causality and potential paradoxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? a few other gamelines already have powers who cause such alterations (like mage (if I remember mage correctly) and demons in nwod as examples (in demons nwod you can even move to the beginning of a scene with specfiic powers or alter scenes/creating alternate scenes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T11:39:11-08:00","id":82183,"title":"","content":"I haven't played either of those gamelines, so I can't say with certainty, but unless a lot of time-related powers were worded very carefully, you could very easily run into something like the grandfather paradox, and you start getting butterfly effects that I at least, as a ST who wants things to work in a pretty plausible manner, just couldn't work out. They'd be too complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T21:44:21-08:00","id":85831,"title":"","content":"I'd like to make a character more in-line with a mage/wizard archetype. Ya know? I've made a few characters with Scion(played even less, because groups are a PITA to find) and I find it VERY hard to make a character that FEELS like a mage or wizard. Either combat, or utility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2454-kyris","name":"Kyris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T23:29:47-08:00","id":85859,"title":"","content":"That's because of a fundamental difference between Scion and &quot;Fantasy&quot; RPGs. In most Fantasy games, &quot;Magic&quot; is a thing that only SOME characters do. In Scion, ALL characters have magic, do magic and <i>are</i> magic. You want to throw fireballs? Learn Fire. Raise Zombies? Death. Summon beasts? Animal. Waterbend like Katara? Water. Smite people with lightning? Sky.<br /> <br /> You can do everything a typical fantasy wizard can do, but it's not in one &quot;Wizard&quot; set of powers. Everyone in Scion is a wizard. You can't specialize in magic, except by specializing in Purviews. Admittedly, the system does make it hard to bypass Epic Attributes because they are hands-down BETTER than Purviews and are, in fact, REQUIRED to use Purviews on-level. So, there are some flaws (big ones, tons of them), but not being able to play a magician isn't one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:29:16-08:00","id":85963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=85859#post85859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because of a fundamental difference between Scion and &quot;Fantasy&quot; RPGs. In most Fantasy games, &quot;Magic&quot; is a thing that only SOME characters do. In Scion, ALL characters have magic, do magic and <i>are</i> magic. You want to throw fireballs? Learn Fire. Raise Zombies? Death. Summon beasts? Animal. Waterbend like Katara? Water. Smite people with lightning? Sky.<br /> <br /> You can do everything a typical fantasy wizard can do, but it's not in one &quot;Wizard&quot; set of powers. Everyone in Scion is a wizard. You can't specialize in magic, except by specializing in Purviews. Admittedly, the system does make it hard to bypass Epic Attributes because they are hands-down BETTER than Purviews and are, in fact, REQUIRED to use Purviews on-level. So, there are some flaws (big ones, tons of them), but not being able to play a magician isn't one.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, then, it sounds like something that Purviews should do is be able to compete with Epic Attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T07:32:25-08:00","id":85998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=85963#post85963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, then, it sounds like something that Purviews should do is be able to compete with Epic Attributes?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, it's more like epic attributes really need to be toned down, definitely the physical attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T08:44:47-08:00","id":86037,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=85998#post85998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, it's more like epic attributes really need to be toned down, definitely the physical attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't like the idea of scaling down the epics. Sorry, but I don't want to give up my ability to rip the Empire State Building out of the ground and chuck it at my enemy. THAT'S what being a mythic hero should feel like.<br /> <br /> <br /> But totally agree with Aranis. What needs to be done is there needs to be something in place that allows Purviews to be just as good a path to extreme power as the epic attributes.<br /> <br /> The idea should be &quot;If you want to be a &quot;caster&quot; who just throws Boons around, you can. If you want to be more of a Herculean paragon of human capability, you can. Ideally, you probably want to strike a balance between these two concepts in order to create a more rounded character who's ready for just about any situation, but if you want to specialize in either, the system is designed to allow that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I really don't see why an aspiring Fire God NEEDS to have high Epic Manipulation in order to use Fire Boons effectively. Nor do I see why Death wielders NEED high Epic Charisma. A lot of Death Gods aren't real charming, doncha know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:10:39-08:00","id":86052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86037#post86037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the idea of scaling down the epics. Sorry, but I don't want to give up my ability to rip the Empire State Building out of the ground and chuck it at my enemy. THAT'S what being a mythic hero should feel like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This. A thousand times this. Scion is a game of Gods and those who will eventually be Gods, and Gods should be able to blow of a mountaintop with a sneeze. They should be able to move so fast that time stand still. They should be able to take a bomb to the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:40:07-08:00","id":86074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=82183#post82183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played either of those gamelines, so I can't say with certainty, but unless a lot of time-related powers were worded very carefully, you could very easily run into something like the grandfather paradox, and you start getting butterfly effects that I at least, as a ST who wants things to work in a pretty plausible manner, just couldn't work out. They'd be too complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, while there DOES need to be a Time purview (for various reasons) the temporal paradox/causality loop thing shouldn't be an issue till you get to God level. Messing with the established timestream is an act that sounds like it goes against Fate, which the one thing Gods CANNOT do. Even if you had the ability to change the recent past (something further back than a few minutes) that ability would not emerge till Avatar-expression level powers. And once you get to that level you're just working in terms of narrative anyway.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Unnatural1: Sorry, but I don't want to give up my ability to rip the Empire State Building out of the ground and chuck it at my enemy. THAT'S what being a mythic hero should feel like.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Omnipotence! Got to get me some of that....<br /> <br /> ((sorry, can't figure out why it won;t auto-quote 2 ppl...))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 03-07-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T10:58:46-08:00","id":86125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86074#post86074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, while there DOES need to be a Time purview (for various reasons) the temporal paradox/causality loop thing shouldn't be an issue till you get to God level. Messing with the established timestream is an act that sounds like it goes against Fate, which the one thing Gods CANNOT do. Even if you had the ability to change the recent past (something further back than a few minutes) that ability would not emerge till Avatar-expression level powers. And once you get to that level you're just working in terms of narrative anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You make a valid point. However, beyond Time-travel type stuff (and its inherent problems) I'm not quite sure what a full powerset of a time purview would look like, especially if it has to be differentiated from Prophecy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T11:12:28-08:00","id":86128,"title":"","content":"While I would find a Time Purview interesting, I don't really think it's a priority or even a necessity (YMMV). Time Gods are rare. Time Gods that actually DO anything with their domain (or really, do anything at all) are rare to the point of non-existence.<br /> <br /> What I really want to see is a Love Purview. Love Gods exist and are an important part of mythology, and Love Gods actually go around making people fall in love and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T12:46:47-08:00","id":86192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86074#post86074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, while there DOES need to be a Time purview (for various reasons)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you name some of those reasons? I've been thinking about the idea of a Time Purview and whether or not to try and find a place for one in my game, and I actually can't quite seem to wrap my head around what it would really do, especially when it comes to historical mythological examples. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:09:34-08:00","id":86253,"title":"","content":"Until modern (like 19th century) science fiction started thinking of time as a thing that could <i>be</i> manipulated, it really wasn't. It was a pattern of cycles, or a thing that just passed. Gods of &quot;time&quot; are pretty often Gods of calendars or Gods or seasons, or years or ages. They don't freeze time, slow time, speed time or anything like that. A Time Purview is pretty much a modern invention, which seems out of place in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:20:29-08:00","id":86260,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head...<br /> <br /> <u>Why a Time purview</u>:<br /> -There ARE Time gods, and titans (yes they\u2019re rare, but they do exist). And such beings would have to be something other than gods who do nothing but chronicle everything.<br /> -Time is an elemental force of the universe as much as Fire, Death, or Light. And it exists beyond the mere concept of seasons.<br /> -About half the powers under the Stars purview do not belong there.<br /> <br /> <u>What would it do</u>?<br /> -Transfer: Perfect Timing, Sense Age, Still Object, Twist Time, and Frozen Moment to this new purview<br /> -Split: Twist time into slow and haste as opposed to both at once.<br /> -Add the following effects:<br /> Hindsight (Prophecy deals with the future, Mystery deals with the present, this would see into the past)<br /> Preserve (remove something/someone from the process of decay. There are stories of those cursed with immortality, so here you go\u2026)<br /> Erode (do the opposite, see Hades in the recent Clash of the Titans remake), Reset (undo last action)<br /> Repeat(repeat last event)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:25:55-08:00","id":86265,"title":"","content":"Those Time Gods are, as discussed, not gods of time <i>travel</i> or time <i>manipulation</i> but simply of time's <i>passage</i>. They don't do anything with that power. There are no stories of things frozen in time, or where a God stops time, travels forward or backward in time, or anything like that. The closest anything comes is how some places run on a different scale of time (Ryujin's palace, faerie holds) but that's more of a feature of a Sanctum or Terra Incognita than a Boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:23:05-08:00","id":86308,"title":"","content":"The only way you can really play a Wizard character right now is to use one of the epic purview systems that are floating around.<br /> Otherwise you are straight jacketed into epic attributes, which can force your character to be something you don't want.<br /> I really hope they do something like the epic purview system in 2nd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:37:12-08:00","id":86325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86253#post86253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until modern (like 19th century) science fiction started thinking of time as a thing that could <i>be</i> manipulated, it really wasn't. It was a pattern of cycles, or a thing that just passed. Gods of &quot;time&quot; are pretty often Gods of calendars or Gods or seasons, or years or ages. They don't freeze time, slow time, speed time or anything like that. A Time Purview is pretty much a modern invention, which seems out of place in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all very true, however Scion does seem to take modern innovation into account. I highly doubt the mythical ancients thought about the concept of gravitation, yet that's a feature of Sun (Inexorable Gravity), as is the idea of molecular fusion (Fusion), and EMPs (Solar Prominence). In one of the Stars powers that actually belongs there (Starfire) we have an extra note about cosmic radiation which hadn't been discovered in the time of the gods but is a feature of the power. Property Infusion from Earth can be written off, but it's getting pretty modern in its descriptive terminology. Unlikely Pattern is clearly based on chaos theory. There aren't a lot of examples but it seems like they were trying to incorporate various modern ideas into this game regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:02:52-08:00","id":86371,"title":"","content":"Oh, I don't know...To play it out, I would think certain ancients had plenty of knowledge of science. (There's argument of quantum physics being mention in the Vedas) But I should wonder if when reality bends to your whim, how relevant is it.<br /> <br /> And some of the &quot;magic weaponry&quot; of the Hindu deities sure seem like nukes to me. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brahmadanda\" target=\"_blank\">Brahmastra</a><i> Brahma had created a weapon even more powerful than the Brahmastra, called the Brahmashira. The Brahmashira was never used in war, as it had four times more power than the Brahmastra, i.e. Fourth power square, as the name suggests, since Brahma has Four Heads. Only Arjuna and Ashwatthama possessed the knowledge to summon the Brahmashira.[1] The weapon was also believed to cause severe environmental damage. The land where the weapon was used became barren and all life in and around that area ceased to exist, as both men and women became infertile. There was also a severe decrease in rainfall with the land developing cracks, like in a drought. </i><br /> <br /> ------------------------------","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 03-07-2014, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T00:03:01-08:00","id":86546,"title":"","content":"I wanted a Time Purview because it would explain Chronos, who had the purview in the first place, being the Titan of Time and all that. On a personal note, I don't know how much the mechanics will change, but usually, Purviews were based on what your divine parent knew. If Time wasn't part of their purviews, then that's tough luck for your character. Plus, the level of Legend dictated how much you can affect in said Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T01:04:47-08:00","id":86579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86546#post86546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted a Time Purview because it would explain Chronos, who had the purview in the first place, being the Titan of Time and all that. On a personal note, I don't know how much the mechanics will change, but usually, Purviews were based on what your divine parent knew. If Time wasn't part of their purviews, then that's tough luck for your character. Plus, the level of Legend dictated how much you can affect in said Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Greeks had a God for pretty much everything, so trying to give them all Purviews is going to be a nightmare (I wouldn't want to the the one designing a Satire Purview for Momus, or a Penis Purview for Priapus, would you?). And besides, Chronos does, literally, absolutely nothing in Greek Mythology, so there's nothing that needs explanation.<br /> <br /> Also, I think you have the rules mixed up a bit. You can learn any Purview you want. Having it associated just gives you an xp discount for buying it. Children of Poseidon can totally learn Fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T07:26:09-08:00","id":86744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86546#post86546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted a Time Purview because it would explain Chronos, who had the purview in the first place, being the Titan of Time and all that. On a personal note, I don't know how much the mechanics will change, but usually, Purviews were based on what your divine parent knew. If Time wasn't part of their purviews, then that's tough luck for your character. Plus, the level of Legend dictated how much you can affect in said Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronos is interesting, since like Gaia, everyone lives with it. Hard to have an opponent that as a concept if beaten takes eternity with it.<br /> <br /> Hmm..seems to me that there are titans that I think it can be said that the gods have an armistice with.<br /> <br /> As a purview though I would look at dimensionality since that's part of the time continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:36:59-08:00","id":86813,"title":"","content":"Again, the &quot;time continuum&quot; is not something that ancient mythology recognized as existing. Yes, Scion has some modern Boons... but they're generally kinda terrible anyway. I think a PC might innovate some modern Boons, but a whole Purview for a concept that's only existed for 200 years? That seems pretty darn out of place. It'd be like a Nuclear Purview or a Black Hole Purview (neither of which I think are good ideas). <br /> <br /> Chronos doesn't freeze time, stop time, twist time or manipulate time. He IS time. In the sense that he's the PASSING of time, he's a creature of seasons, days, nights, years, etc. He doesn't do HG Wells, Star Trek or Magic: the Gathering type time manipulation. He just embodies the idea of time being a thing that passes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:40:24-08:00","id":86901,"title":"","content":"And yet with every other incarnation of Chronos, from the past to Percy Jackson, writers wrote that Chronos dealt with Time as a fact. Hell, in The Last Olympian, they had Chronos LITERALLY affected Time by slowing down the Olympians so that his forces could pick them off. Plus,the concept of time has been around for perhaps over 3,000 years, not 200. Evidence of people trying to understand it came from attempts including the Sundial and the Water Clock and the Hourglass.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that Nuclear power would either be placed in the Sun purview (because of it being a force of light) and/or War (because of World War II). And as for a Black Hole Purview, I think they covered that in the Chaos Purview by using the Void Avatar, because Black Holes are essentially voids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:02:48-08:00","id":86916,"title":"","content":"Y'know, that would be kinda cool to have a nuclear detonation stopped cold by the Void. Guy pops back from avatar form and belches smoke..<i>&quot;scuse me..but that was one spicy meatball!&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T12:05:30-08:00","id":86920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86901#post86901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet with every other incarnation of Chronos, from the past to Percy Jackson, writers wrote that Chronos dealt with Time as a fact. Hell, in The Last Olympian, they had Chronos LITERALLY affected Time by slowing down the Olympians so that his forces could pick them off. Plus,the concept of time has been around for perhaps over 3,000 years, not 200. Evidence of people trying to understand it came from attempts including the Sundial and the Water Clock and the Hourglass.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that Nuclear power would either be placed in the Sun purview (because of it being a force of light) and/or War (because of World War II). And as for a Black Hole Purview, I think they covered that in the Chaos Purview by using the Void Avatar, because Black Holes are essentially voids.</div> </div> </div> </div>That aspect of Percy Jackson is inaccurate. Plain and simple. Also, Chronos does not appear in Percy Jackson. Cronus, Titan of Agriculture and father of Zeus, Poseidon and Hades, does. I suppose giving him Fertility powers like he should have had would not have made a very interesting villain.<br /> <br /> The concept of time has been around since Time began. But the concept of playing around with Time is modern, not mythic. Besides, by these arguments, why do we even have a Sun Purview? Modern science is well aware that the Sun is but another Star; we could just give Apollo and Ra and all the others Stars and be done with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Upon further reflection, I feel like I'm giving off the wrong impression here. Firstly, I love Rick Riordan's work. I just also know that he conflated Chronos and Cronus, who are completely different figures in Greek myth and I will call him out on it.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't really think having a Time Purview breaks the game. I just a. Strongly agree with Telgar that most Science type Boons in RAW were fairly underwhelming and anti-thematic and a Time Purview would have the same problems, and b. There are more important mythic powers that need representation first (Love and Artistry), things that Gods in myth actually actively DO!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-09-2014, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T13:55:45-07:00","id":89028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86920#post86920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. There are more important mythic powers that need representation first (Love and Artistry), things that Gods in myth actually actively DO!</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with a love (or other emotional) purview (in scion 1e at least) always was in my oppinion that many of the things I would expect in it were already covered by knacks :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:07:14-07:00","id":89084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86920#post86920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept of time has been around since Time began. But the concept of playing around with Time is modern, not mythic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid I must challenge that statement.<br /> <br /> Folk stories sometimes mention places where time passes faster or slower, with the protagonists returning only to find that either years have passed or no time at all. The fair folk and places associated with them were notorious for this.<br /> <br /> Curses that cause someone to age to infirmity or death are also something that crops up in myths.<br /> <br /> I could swear I remember hearing at least one old folk tale about a man managing to wander backwards in time as well. I can't find anything definite on this subject from before the 1700s though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths-legends-unexplained-phenomena/time-travel-ancient-mythology-modern-science-001242\" target=\"_blank\">This article</a> mentions a few good examples of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1218,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","user":"Taejix","date":". 03-11-2014, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1218-taejix","name":"Taejix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:40:22-07:00","id":89113,"title":"","content":"Hmm...maybe break some of them down. I guess I'm looking at the Muses; Calliope (Epic poetry; Symbol=Writing tablet); Clio (History; Symbol=Scrolls); Erato (Lyric Poetry; Symbol=Cithara); Euterpe (Song and Elegiac poetry; Symbol=Aulos); Melpomene (Tragedy Symbol=Tragic mask); Polyhymnia (Hymns Symbol=Veil); Terpsichore (Dance Symbol=Lyre); Thalia (Comedy Symbol=Comic mask); Urania (Astronomy Symbol=Globe and compass) Kind of like having sub-purviews. But I think this idea has been explored earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:41:47-07:00","id":89163,"title":"","content":"Most stories of 'time travel' in ancient myth are exactly what that article mentions: time moving in different rates inside magical places. I don't think that's enough to warrant a whole Purview, especially since those places are rarely connected to the few &quot;Time&quot; Gods that do exist. Ryujin, for example, has <i>nothing</i> to do with time and neither do the fae. Age, the coming of weathering, rust and decrepitude, is more of a <i>result</i> of time and better embodied by Death.<br /> <br /> What could a Time Purview do that's mythically resonant except age things and make time move differently in other worlds (generally just a property of that <i>being a different world</i> with different rules)? Enough for a fully developed Purview with 20 or so Boons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T18:47:20-07:00","id":89166,"title":"","content":"Maybe some are looking at Doctor Who?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T21:27:14-07:00","id":89238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taejix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=89084#post89084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid I must challenge that statement.<br /> <br /> Folk stories sometimes mention places where time passes faster or slower, with the protagonists returning only to find that either years have passed or no time at all. The fair folk and places associated with them were notorious for this.<br /> <br /> Curses that cause someone to age to infirmity or death are also something that crops up in myths.<br /> <br /> I could swear I remember hearing at least one old folk tale about a man managing to wander backwards in time as well. I can't find anything definite on this subject from before the 1700s though.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.ancient-origins.net/myths-legends-unexplained-phenomena/time-travel-ancient-mythology-modern-science-001242\" target=\"_blank\">This article</a> mentions a few good examples of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The article was interesting, and thank you for it, but all of those examples are variations on the same theme: a place where time flows differently, not a God actively doing anything (with the possible exception of the Christian myth), and is thus probably better represented by the Sanctum Birthright.<br /> <br /> In addition, the power to age someone to infirmity already exists in the game...in the Health Purview, as Control Ageing, where it fits perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T16:10:28-07:00","id":89801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=86265#post86265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Time Gods are, as discussed, not gods of time <i>travel</i> or time <i>manipulation</i> but simply of time's <i>passage</i>. They don't do anything with that power. There are no stories of things frozen in time, or where a God stops time, travels forward or backward in time, or anything like that. The closest anything comes is how some places run on a different scale of time (Ryujin's palace, faerie holds) but that's more of a feature of a Sanctum or Terra Incognita than a Boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>..But, isn't the entire point of Scion that the gods change and grow with common beliefs?<br /> <br /> there was an entire expansion adding things like the &quot;yankee pantheon&quot;, so it seems clear to me that scion is a bit less cut and dry about what fits in where when it comes to mythology and categorizations. I mean, it would be easy enough to fit &quot;father time&quot; in a pantheon the same way they did paul bunyon, with a &quot;time purview&quot; to go along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2454-kyris","name":"Kyris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T17:01:57-07:00","id":89824,"title":"","content":"ok...I don't think it would fit, so perhaps some examples on how a Time Purview would work? I'm looking at Mage the Ascension and thinking of &quot;Wrinkle&quot; and it's not pretty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T14:12:50-07:00","id":90418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=89801#post89801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ..But, isn't the entire point of Scion that the gods change and grow with common beliefs?<br /> <br /> there was an entire expansion adding things like the &quot;yankee pantheon&quot;, so it seems clear to me that scion is a bit less cut and dry about what fits in where when it comes to mythology and categorizations. I mean, it would be easy enough to fit &quot;father time&quot; in a pantheon the same way they did paul bunyon, with a &quot;time purview&quot; to go along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've actually hit on a rather large point of contention among Scion fans. Some would emphatically say that, YES! Human belief shapes the Gods and they should evolve along with modern culture. Others (who tend to be a bit more numerous at least on the forums and among those that create Scion fan-material) say NO! the Gods exist independent of human belief and are NOT shaped by that. They can be influenced by Fatebindings, but they don't actually change in response to pop culture. Their own <i>actions</i> create Fatebonds, not just mortals making up stories about them out of boredom. Thor isn't influenced by the Avengers, Heracles doesn't care about Kevin Sorbo. <br /> <br /> I err more strongly on the side of Scion being about ancient mythology coming <i>into</i> the modern world, not being updated <i>for</i> the modern world. You may take a different approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T17:02:20-07:00","id":90506,"title":"","content":"It is a pretty fine line, but I come down mostly on the end of gods being shaped by sincere human belief. Thor is not affected by Marvel, because nobody (or an incredibly tiny number of people) actually believe that that version is a deity. In modern terms, it pretty much means that if we take the world as it is right now, really only the Deva are being actively influenced by human belief. However, if the &quot;Masquerade&quot; is broken, things may change. Pop culture and religion are not the same thing, and as much as Scion deals with mythology as a thing that 'happened in the past' it also is a game about religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T17:11:11-07:00","id":90511,"title":"","content":"The Yazata, Shinto and Orisha/Loa also have active current, and non-reconstructivist religions. There are also followers of reconstructed versions of pretty much all the other Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T17:32:01-07:00","id":90520,"title":"","content":"Chinese folk religion is also flourishing. Both on the mainland and in the Chinese Diaspora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T21:26:18-07:00","id":90635,"title":"","content":"Knew I forgot someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T16:00:06-07:00","id":91156,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess my information on modern practices and revivals of the kind of traditional religion that Scion focuses on is rather lacking. I still think that my criteria for the relationship between deities and human belief is entirely reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T03:50:57-07:00","id":91529,"title":"","content":"To me, one important thing is that purviews actually aren't just a set of powers that are arbitrarily plucked together to form a purview. I'd like to see actual control over the purview itself beyond just avatar abilities.<br /> <br /> Let those who master fire control normal fire already at low legend. A scion with sky caught in a thunderstorm? Let him try to appease the storm.<br /> <br /> In my house rules I've differed &quot;legendary&quot; from &quot;mortal&quot;. A fire demigod can control fire that is mortal and natural, but not fire that is legendary (i.e. overworld fire and other fire boons). A tad bit more flexible boon system would be awesome, as long as it doesn't devolve into &quot;Mage&quot; as I have players that argue that system to death every time we try to play it (&quot;but I have forces one and here's the reason I should be able to create a black hole...&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T05:10:12-07:00","id":91553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91529#post91529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, one important thing is that purviews actually aren't just a set of powers that are arbitrarily plucked together to form a purview. I'd like to see actual control over the purview itself beyond just avatar abilities.<br /> <br /> Let those who master fire control normal fire already at low legend. A scion with sky caught in a thunderstorm? Let him try to appease the storm.<br /> <br /> In my house rules I've differed &quot;legendary&quot; from &quot;mortal&quot;. A fire demigod can control fire that is mortal and natural, but not fire that is legendary (i.e. overworld fire and other fire boons). A tad bit more flexible boon system would be awesome, as long as it doesn't devolve into &quot;Mage&quot; as I have players that argue that system to death every time we try to play it (&quot;but I have forces one and here's the reason I should be able to create a black hole...&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>In their defence, those types of powers <i>did</i> exist...they were, admittedly very all over the place; really, how come controlling Water was level two, while Fire was level eight? And by all that is holy, why is controlling the Sky not possible in any meaningful way before level ten?<br /> <br /> I see two small problems with powers that are too flexible. Firstly, it leads to situations like the Water Purview, which effectively has the exact same Boon repeated thrice with a few more extras attached each time. This makes it a bit boring in my opinion. The other thing I dislike about them is that they end up making older powers feel redundant. Human Clay, in Health, can effectively do anything the Boons before it can do, and more. These are, of course, more personal gripes than any actual criticism of the mechanics.<br /> <br /> However, one thing I <i>would</i> very much like to see is Avatars made more impactful. As of now, there amazing one trick ponies, but I would like to see attaining the Avatar of a Purview do more than just add to your list of associations. I would like it if they gave passive bonuses to Boon use in that Purview, because as it stands, any random Legend 12 God who picks up a Water Boon is as good at it as a dedicated Water God like Poseidon or Sarasvati.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 03-15-2014, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T07:36:42-07:00","id":91618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91553#post91553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...how come controlling Water was level two, while Fire was level eight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, it makes sense. Looking at classical belief in the elements, fire was the most unpredictable and most difficult to control of all elements. It was also in fire's nature to destroy <i>itself</i> by consuming everything that fuels it while the other three classical elements exist of their own merit. Bolster Fire fixes that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Human Clay, in Health, can effectively do anything the Boons before it can do... </div> </div> </div>Except be used in the places it matters most, without (A) requiring a god <i>not</i> avatar down and therefore cause Fate to come knocking in a big, big way, and (B) spending enough Legend to cause an horrific number and level of Fatebonds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T08:31:19-07:00","id":91656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91618#post91618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thematically, it makes sense. Looking at classical belief in the elements, fire was the most unpredictable and most difficult to control of all elements. It was also in fire's nature to destroy <i>itself</i> by consuming everything that fuels it while the other three classical elements exist of their own merit. Bolster Fire fixes that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's fair to make a generalization like that. To many ancient civilizations, it's often the opposite...Water is the Element of Primordial Chaos, while Fire is the Element of Order and Stability. Brahma is self-born out of the Waters of Chaos and must tame them before Creation can begin. Ra must bring forth the World from the sea of Nun. Marduk must defeat the Waters of Tiamat before the Gods can take their rightful place. In all these cases Water is an uncontrollable force that must be taken to task before the Gods can bring Order. On the other hand, Fire to the Deva and Yazata is the Element of civilization and order. Fire Gods like Atar, Hestia and Agni are important adjuncts to the ruling figures, and Fire is one of the weapons used by Marduk to defeat Tiamat and Zhu Rong to defeat GongGong. It's no accident, after all, that sea Gods are often portrayed as being alien and beyond the normal jurisdictions of their Pantheon. Poseidon goes against his brother all the time, though at least he does get some comeuppance. Ryujin holds his own court separate from Amaterasu's. Varuna is not just the leader of the Asura, he might well have broken off from the Deva to create their arch-nemesis, the Yazata, depending on whether you believe the theory that Varuna is Ahura Mazda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91618#post91618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except be used in the places it matters most, without (A) requiring a god <i>not</i> avatar down and therefore cause Fate to come knocking in a big, big way, and (B) spending enough Legend to cause an horrific number and level of Fatebonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I was not considering it that way. True, any God with half a brain is going to Avatar down on Earth, at which point Human Clay becomes unusable (anyone else feel that the word Avatar gets used to mean way too many things in Scion?). I concede my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T13:32:05-07:00","id":91820,"title":"","content":"Good analysis, Griffinguy. I wish I had the time to attempt something similar. <br /> <br /> I posted this before when a similar topic came up, but it seems relevant. <br /> <br /> (I apologize if anyone already posted something like this. The forum and my computer still don't get along, meaning I can read only the first and last pages of a thread.) <br /> <br /> I\u2019d recommend getting rid of the \u201cSpecial Purview\u201d category. I know from experience that players have enough trouble keeping straight the difference between buying PSPs a dot at a time and buying APP Boons singly. Special Purviews are a needless complication. It is also objectively stupid, or at least a waste of XP, to buy more than one dot in either Mystery or Prophecy. <br /> <br /> Instead, I would create a new APP called Oracle. Mystery and Prophecy would be single Boons within the APP (and likely rewritten a bit). Oracle would also subsume all the divinatory spells from Magic, such as Ariadne\u2019s Thread or Unlidded Eye. <br /> <br /> Remaining spells would go in other new APPs. The probability-controlling spells such as Bona Fortuna and Evil Eye would become Boons in the Purview of Fate \u2013 or more accurately, Fate and Chance, as all the probability-related Boons from Chaos (such as Eye of the Storm and Hornet\u2019s Nest) would go here as well. <br /> <br /> Chaos is redefined as the Purview of madness, illusion, and generally breaking or warping consciousness, perception and (at higher levels) the rules of reality. IMO this makes it more representative for Gods of frenzy and intoxication such as Dionysus, or deception such as Loki. The new Chaos can swallow the Illusion Purview, if you like. <br /> <br /> There can still be a Magic Purview, but this APP deals more with direct manipulation of Legend, transformation and the interactions between Legendary creatures and mundane reality. Examples would be Legendary Surge, Blood Mead (a transformation, transferring Abilities between characters) or Legendary Beacon (a proposed Boon that simply sends out a signal to every creature of Legend in a wide area, letting them know another creature of Legend wants to meet them). Maybe Boons for sympathetic magic, too, though this could create overlap with other Purviews. (But I think it\u2019s okay if some Boons can fit in more than one Purview.) <br /> <br /> [EDIT: In view of Telgar's analysis, I am not even sure there should be a Purview called &quot;Magic.&quot;] <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also add an APP of Craft or Artifice, for reasons that should be obvious to anyone who knows their mythology. <br /> <br /> As it stands, Fertility deals with plants. Period. Can we just call it the Plant Purview? <br /> <br /> I have no serious problems with any of the other APPs, though plenty of Boons should be revised or replaced. [EDIT: Some Purviews, such as Moon, will probably have to remain grab-bags of oddball Boons, just because they don't lend themselves to easy, coherent sets of powers the way, say, Fire, Sky, or Guardian do. I can live with it.] <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T11:43:45-07:00","id":92376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91656#post91656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I was not considering it that way. True, any God with half a brain is going to Avatar down on Earth, at which point Human Clay becomes unusable (anyone else feel that the word Avatar gets used to mean way too many things in Scion?). I concede my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Avatar is way too ambiguous of a word in this game, yes.<br /> <br /> My current kludge fix for the &quot;gods ratcheting down their Legend temporarily&quot; mechanic is to call it &quot;manifestation.&quot; Once you're Legend 9+, your natural plane of existence is the Overworld, and you hang out there at whatever Legend you are, just like the way you existed in the World previously. When you want to interact with your old playground anymore, you Manifest there temporarily, at a Legend level you select. (Manifesting at Legend 1 is the cheap, almost no-risk &quot;ghost of Obi-Wan&quot; sort of Manifestation, where you can walk around, talk, be visible, etc. but not really interact with the World or have it interact with you; ideal for Visitations or directing your mortal minions, whatevs.) The &quot;Avatar&quot; birthright is not a thing anymore, and Manifesting at various Legend levels is something all gods just have the ability to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1160-luminous-crayon","name":"Luminous Crayon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T11:48:13-07:00","id":92381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=91656#post91656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it's fair to make a generalization like that. To many ancient civilizations, it's often the opposite...Water is the Element of Primordial Chaos, while Fire is the Element of Order and Stability. Brahma is self-born out of the Waters of Chaos and must tame them before Creation can begin. Ra must bring forth the World from the sea of Nun. Marduk must defeat the Waters of Tiamat before the Gods can take their rightful place. In all these cases Water is an uncontrollable force that must be taken to task before the Gods can bring Order. On the other hand, Fire to the Deva and Yazata is the Element of civilization and order. Fire Gods like Atar, Hestia and Agni are important adjuncts to the ruling figures, and Fire is one of the weapons used by Marduk to defeat Tiamat and Zhu Rong to defeat GongGong. It's no accident, after all, that sea Gods are often portrayed as being alien and beyond the normal jurisdictions of their Pantheon. Poseidon goes against his brother all the time, though at least he does get some comeuppance. Ryujin holds his own court separate from Amaterasu's. Varuna is not just the leader of the Asura, he might well have broken off from the Deva to create their arch-nemesis, the Yazata, depending on whether you believe the theory that Varuna is Ahura Mazda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aztec stuff works similarly, in that the world was formed from the defeat of an aquatic monster (which Tezcatlipoca had to lure by sticking his foot into the water to be eaten) before the gods could create land. Fire reinforces order by playing a role in sacrifice to the gods, transmitting power. It's also literally the weapon that Huitzilopochtli wields to drive back night; the sun's rays are his spears, and the atlatl he hurls them with is the serpent alter-ego of the god of the hearth.<br /> <br /> The idea the Varuna is also Ahura Mazda is blowing my mind, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1160-luminous-crayon","name":"Luminous Crayon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T06:47:14-07:00","id":99972,"title":"","content":"I strongly support the suggestion to disentangle Epic Attributes from Purviews, and that includes removing attributes from the dicepools for them - it just pigeonholes a god of Death into Charisma, even if it's bloody Hel.<br /> <br /> I have a point pertaining to that that hasn't been made yet:<br /> <br /> It has to be decided of purviews should be focused on a specific purpose or flexible. What I mean to say is: In the current system, as a god of Fertility, your combat and social utility is basically nil. As a god of Frost, you have a respectable amount of combat boons, but just one social power and little that is useful in shaping the world at large to your purposes - even if freezing a field of crops isn't a god-level power, it just isn't there earlier. It has been theorized by many that the official boons are just examples and you could write combat boons for Fertility or more social boons for Frost (I think GBN did just that).<br /> <br /> Both perspectives are acceptable, but I suggest that the decision should be made once and for all, and then executed with utmost consequence. If my divine purview of Death is to be useful to me in combat, social confrontation, and manipulating the setting at large, then this has to be built in from the start, with boons to support all of these purposes at all levels as is appropriate for the Purview.<br /> If, on the other hand, purviews should inherently support only one or two areas of application, that should also be done with consequence, and there should be NO social boon for the Fire purview, and useful Boons for both combat and elemental shaping at any level.<br /> <br /> The current situation - with some purviews having a clear vision in their design and some just being all over the place of possible uses - makes it very hard for players to decide on just what your character should also be good at if he is to be a future Sun god. Either purviews are useful for all areas of expertise, or they should come with a clear focus to build a character around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:33:45-07:00","id":101066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/74082-what-should-each-purview-do-in-2e?p=89113#post89113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...maybe break some of them down. I guess I'm looking at the Muses; Calliope (Epic poetry; Symbol=Writing tablet); Clio (History; Symbol=Scrolls); Erato (Lyric Poetry; Symbol=Cithara); Euterpe (Song and Elegiac poetry; Symbol=Aulos); Melpomene (Tragedy Symbol=Tragic mask); Polyhymnia (Hymns Symbol=Veil); Terpsichore (Dance Symbol=Lyre); Thalia (Comedy Symbol=Comic mask); Urania (Astronomy Symbol=Globe and compass) Kind of like having sub-purviews. But I think this idea has been explored earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>And don't forget the fabled 10TH MUSE from Blue Water Comics (Ba Dum Kssh!) Personally, it would be interesting to use the 10th Muse as plot in a Scion game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}